        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/greywind/{size}/2006_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-21T18:17:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"LevelUpLeo\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/levelupleo/48/2394_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> LevelUpLeo:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There are pleanty of things in the Sentinels Universe that are \"forces of nature\" but are still targets. Just cause it's a \"force of nature\" doesn't meant mankind doesn't need to be protected from it.&nbsp;As for saving the Galactus villain for the last set, yeah, I see how that makes sense, but he would fit really well with this theme. If he were to be in the last expansion too, it would pretty much have to be another space based one, which seems a little redundant.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Just because it's a target and mankind needs protecting from it, that doesn't make it a villain.</p>",
